    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "A claim is revised · 2",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to follow a change in stance after a relevant objection.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-28-required-interaction-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Respond to the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-28-required-interaction-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "A claim is revised · 2: A partner proposes acting immediately on the first part of this account. Explain the later information they need, ask one clarification, and negotiate a suitable next step.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "朋友看见我桌子上的书，想借回家。我说这本是同学的，我说了明天还。他说只看一天，明天早上一定给我，问我为什么不马上说好。\n\n我说：“不是说好明天还吗？我得先问同学，他的书不是我想借给谁就借给谁。”朋友听懂了，说可以等我问，不急着拿走。\n\n同学在电话里说可以借，但明天一定要还，因为下午上课要用。我把这个时间告诉朋友，他说会在早上送来，不会让同学上课没有书。\n\n第二天早上，朋友把书送来了，说里面的故事很好。我说：“这本书是很有用的，可它不是我的。下次你可以自己问同学借。”\n\n下午我把书还给同学，也告诉他朋友很喜欢。三个人都清楚书在哪里、什么时候还，所以同学上课的时候能用书。能帮朋友，也要做到对同学说过的事。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "My reply uses the later information instead of simply repeating the first claim."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "My clarification and proposed next step address the practical constraint."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
